(
 'Compares two versions of a given file or APL object, taken from two different commits'
 ''
 'Takes one mandatory and one optional argument'
 ''
 '* The mandatory argument must specify either an APL object or a filename. Filenames are'
 '  relative to the ROOT of the project; see -??? for the full rule.'
 '     '
 '* The optional argument, when specified, must be one of:'
 '  * An integer smaller than 10000000; treated as maximum number of hashes to be displayed'
 '    for selection by the user.'
 '  * An integer larger than 10000000; expected to be YYYYMMDD and interpreted as "display'
 '    all hashes up to and including the given date".'
 '  * A simple character vector; treated as "hash1,hash2". No hash list is presented then.'
 ''
 'If the user command ]CompareFiles and its API is available then this is used'
 'for the comparison. Otherwise the names of two files are printed to the session.'
 ''
 'The command tries to establish the project itself, but check -project='
 ''
 '-files     If you just want to get filenames printed to ⎕SE specify this modifier'
 '-use=      Use this to specify a particular comparison utility; see ]CompareFiles for details.'
 '-project=  Use this to specify a specific folder that hosts a project  '
 ''
)
